Z||000000||maryjane||07-20-2001||06:04 PM||||I went to buy a new rad cap today cause the old one looks a little ragged on the rubber seal. I wanted an AC Delco cause they always try to sell me a vented one in Stant. The box has this on it<BR>ACD# RC27<BR>GM# 10409635<BR>15psi<BR>It is supposed to be non-vented but the cap has 2 arrows opposite each other and say "align vent with hose" Does that mean it is vented? <BR>84se 2.5<BR>confused||||reg||9
Z||000001||Rodrv6||07-20-2001||06:14 PM||||It's not vented---one of the arrows will align with the line that vents the radiator to the overflow tank when the cap is installed and turned all the way.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
